From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Stockdale <jstockdale@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:23:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: touchscreen
 physical size in the controller frame

Ours (2026-11-02, A.3 stylus), after the Fedora iceland port's board patch
(mzak, "give the touchscreen its physical size"): the common touchscreen-x-mm
/ touchscreen-y-mm properties let the nt36536 driver set a resolution on the
touch and pen axes, which libinput requires before it accepts the pen as a
tablet and the compositors use for the touch-to-output mapping. Exit: submit
to Perpetua together with the two driver patches.

The panel's active area is 274 x 193 mm (the panel driver reports it on the
DSI connector; 3392 x 2400 px). The touch controller's own frame is portrait,
the one touchscreen-size-x = 24000 / touchscreen-size-y = 33920 describe: the
stock device tree gives that range to the finger and the pen alike
(touchpanel,panel-coords = touchpanel,pen-panel-coords = <0x5dc0 0x8480>)
against touchpanel,display-coords = <0x960 0xd40> (2400 x 3392, ten units per
pixel). The lengths belong to the controller's axes, like the sizes: its X
axis (24000 units) runs along the panel's 193 mm short side, its Y axis
(33920 units) along the 274 mm long side, and touchscreen-swapped-x-y (after
touchscreen-inverted-x) turns that into the panel's landscape frame. The
Fedora board file carries the opposite pairing (x-mm = 274, y-mm = 193)
because its driver hard-codes the swap and registers the axes in the
landscape frame already; ours describes the controller, as the size
properties do.

The driver pairs each registered axis with the length of the controller axis
it carries (the lengths are swapped together with the ranges), so both
devices end up with 33920 / 274 = 124 units/mm on the landscape X axis and
24000 / 193 = 124 units/mm on the Y axis (123.8 and 124.4 before rounding),
the scale of ten units per pixel on a 3392 x 2400 px panel of 274 x 193 mm.

Signed-off-by: John Stockdale <jstockdale@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index 6e907e4c8f2b..2f55b7f8c494 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -1315,6 +1315,15 @@ touchscreen@0 {
 		touchscreen-size-y = <33920>;
 		touchscreen-inverted-x;
 		touchscreen-swapped-x-y;
+
+		/*
+		 * Physical size in the controller's own (portrait) frame: its X
+		 * axis, 24000 units, runs along the panel's 193 mm short side and
+		 * its Y axis, 33920 units, along the 274 mm long side; the swap
+		 * above turns the frame into the panel's landscape one.
+		 */
+		touchscreen-x-mm = <193>;
+		touchscreen-y-mm = <274>;
 	};
 };
 
